Round 25 (2026-02-27)

What landed
- Files changed:
  - `clang/aot/emit.c`
- Added an expression-level OP2 fold path (non-head `aot_emit_node(..., OP2)`):
  - still emits structural lhs/rhs terms;
  - when `STEPS_ITRS_LIM == 0`, if tags are already WHNF:
    - `ERA` lhs -> `wnf_op2_era()`
    - `NUM` lhs + `ERA` rhs -> `wnf_op2_num_era()`
    - `NUM` lhs + `NUM` rhs -> `wnf_op2_num_num_raw(...)`
    - otherwise keep `term_new_op2(...)`
  - when `STEPS_ITRS_LIM != 0`, preserves old structural `term_new_op2(...)`.

Why this mattered
- Round 24 only reduced demanded OP2 materialization; `mat_mul` stayed dominated by expression `TERM_OP2`.
- Many OP2 sites already had NUM/ERA operands at runtime, but we still allocated OP2 nodes.

Validation
- Build: `cd clang && clang -O2 -o main main.c`
- Tests: `./test/_all_.sh` passed.
- Admission-set sweep (`HVM_AOT_DEOPT=1 ... --as-c -s -T1`) stayed deopt-clean:
  - `AOT_DEOPT total=0` on all sampled admission benches.
  - Residuals unchanged/small (`mat_mul` still 3 `EXPR_CTR_FIELD_CAPTURE`; `gab_takl` still 3 residual captures).
- Output parity spot checks (interpreted vs `--as-c`) matched on:
  - `mat_mul`, `u32_fib`, `graph_color`, `prime_sieve`, `tree_fold`, `ray_sphere`.

